Problem restatement:

We have a road of length n positions 0..n-1.

Given array lights of length n. For each i: if lights[i] = v > 0, there is a working bulb at position i that illuminates positions from max(0, i - v) to min(n-1, i + v) inclusive. If lights[i] = 0, there is no working bulb at position i.

A position is visible if illuminated by at least one working bulb.

We may install additional bulbs at any positions. Each additional bulb installed at position j illuminates positions from max(0, j - 1) to min(n-1, j + 1), inclusive (i.e., radius 1 coverage). So each extra bulb covers 3 positions (or less at edges).

Goal: return minimum number of additional bulbs required to make every position on the road visible.

We have to output the method minLights(self, lights: list[int]) -> int in class Solution.

Constraints: n up to 1e5.

We need an algorithm O(n) or O(n log n).

