Since we have intervals [L_i, R_i] for each existing bulb, we can use a sweep line / difference array.

Approach: Initialize diff array of size n+1 with zeros. For each bulb i with v>0: L = max(0, i - v), R = min(n-1, i + v). diff[L] += 1; diff[R+1] -= 1 (if R+1 < n). Then compute prefix sum: cur = 0; for j in 0..n-1: cur += diff[j]; covered[j] = (cur > 0). This is O(n) total.

